Carafe Lab: the OpenGL renderer configures a compute dispatch with the buffer and texture cache locks held, as the
Vulkan renderer does. Without them a dispatch synchronized buffers while a guest thread under NCE reported its write
to the same pages: the upload cleared the CPU-modified bits the write had just set and protected the page again, the
access faulted once more, and the guest's data never reached the GPU (Hitman 2: Silent Assassin's broken geometry,
holes and stale menu pictures).
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -403,6 +403,7 @@ void RasterizerOpenGL::DispatchCompute() {
     if (pipeline->UsesLocalMemory()) {
         program_manager.LocalMemoryWarmup();
     }
+    std::scoped_lock lock{texture_cache.mutex, buffer_cache.mutex};
     pipeline->SetEngine(kepler_compute, gpu_memory);
     pipeline->Configure();
     const auto& qmd{kepler_compute->launch_description};
